The doctor writes the prescription.
Then he looks at me.
Then he smiles.
He says, "There is nothing to worry about."
"This is a viral fever due to the changing weather."
I ask, "Doctor, what should I do?"
The doctor says, "Headache is common in a viral infection."
"I am writing some medicines on a prescription."
He gives me the prescription and also gives some advice.
He says, "You should drink a lot of warm water."
"You should eat only light food."
"And you should rest at home for two days."
I understand his words.
The doctor's words give me courage.
But I feel reassured after talking to the doctor.
I get up from my chair.
I say thank you to him.
Now I have to go to the medical store to get the medicines.
